source	Plato, Euthydemus 293b-d, tr. B. Jowett
text	Project Gutenberg ebook 1598, https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/1598
class	equivocation
word	knowing
fault	"knowing" is knowing some thing in "if you know, you are knowing" and knowing without qualification in "you are not knowing", so that being knowing and not knowing are not contraries
reference	Plato, Euthydemus 293c-d (Socrates' "of the knowledge which I have"); Aristotle, Sophistical Refutations 5, 166b37-167a20
known	canon
